    <div class="post-container" id="fpc-2134517">
                      
		<div class="post" id="post-2134517">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,2134517)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-2134517">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thedeadlymoose" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(732274); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=732274&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608282649" alt="thedeadlymoose" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=732274)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thedeadlymoose" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(732274); return false;" >thedeadlymoose</a></span> <span class="odate time_1413668462 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">18 Oct 2014 21:41</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2134517">
									

<p>Examples of errors:</p>
<ul>
<li>You randomly put no space in between paragraphs. This is grammatically unacceptable and, plainly, sloppy.</li>
<li>Re: the opening: The story is boring &amp; mostly generic until you reach the line “It says that, two days ago, a Mr. Walter Copper died due to a broken spine. Reasons unknown.”</li>
</ul>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>“How is this relevant?” asked Hamilton, who was beginning to think his time was being wasted. Sanchez would be desperate to try and show his command he had his eye on the ball, yet this would just make him look like an idiot.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Relevant to what?</p>
<p>Why all this info dumping? (You should let this be implied, in other words.) And why is Hamilton reacting this way? Doesn't make any sense. You haven't given us the context.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Hamilton was about to laugh at the absurdity of the sentence, when he realized the full implications of what was being said.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a goofy way to react. The implications were clear up-front, and the sentence isn't that absurd from the Foundation's POV.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Hamilton never finished, as Sanchez was clearly desperate to get his point across.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Now you've switched POV to omniscient. Why? (Although, you're barely in Hamilton's POV in the first place.)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Hamilton stood up, knocking over the pot of pens as he did so.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a goofy over-the-top reaction.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>“Has it breached containment?” he asked, his voice a tone of worry.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>As is this, though it's less comedic. Why would a professional react this way? Let alone a professional member of the Foundation? You're giving a DUN DUN DUNNNNNNN moment to a really underwhelming SCP. And even if you were talking about a world-destroying Keter, where the reaction would be <em>justified</em>, I'd still recommend underplaying it for impact.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Hamilton began to relax, but stopped himself just before he did.<br />
“S-sir, I-I think…” began Sanchez, whose voice was filled with worry.<br />
“I think there’s more than one.”</p>
<p>Hamilton stared vacantly at Sanchez, before snapping out of it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Same issue. This is goofy and unprofessional. It's not even childish, because a child wouldn't 'stare vacantly' in reaction to that. (And, too much stuttering.)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>“Alright, have you told anyone else?” he asked hastily.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why would he ask this? Are you trying to imply that Hamilton is in on a plot to spread these objects? Even if he is, you shouldn't use that line &#8212; it's a cliche, and there's literally no reason for this to be kept a secret. Just rephrase.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>“N-no…” said Sanchez, quietly.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Way too much stuttering.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>“What?” said Hamilton impatiently. He grabbed the pen pot and slammed it onto the table, upright.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Again, they're acting like a parody. Just imagine this scene playing out in a real office.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Sanchez jumped up suddenly, making his chair fall on the floor.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This doesn't work with the preceding paragraph; it sounds like Sanchez wasn't paying any attention until Hamilton was done slowly falling over. Also, it's awkwardly phrased.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Sanchez stood in silence, for what could have been either seconds or hours, before finally whispering, &quot;They're everywhere…&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is also really goofy.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><em>Collapsed the wall of text. -Zyn</em></p>
<hr />
<p>I'm stopping here, but hopefully this is instructive, re: how to fix the rest of it as well. The whole thing just really doesn't work very well. I enjoyed the concept that Eskobar pointed out above, but I am unfortunately not compelled enough to upvote.</p>

							</div>

								
